                // From the invariant, we know:
                //   inner.oneshot0_inv_half@ is HalfRightToComplete || Complete

                // Suppose for contradiction that inner.oneshot0_inv_half@ is HalfRightToComplete.
                // Then op(oneshot0_complete@, inner.oneshot0_inv_half@) = op(Complete, HalfRightToComplete) = Invalid.

                // But we have two resources at the same location:
                // - oneshot0_complete at location L
                // - inner.oneshot0_inv_half at location L
                // And we know op(oneshot0_complete@, inner.oneshot0_inv_half@) = Invalid.

                // This is a contradiction because resources at the same location must have
                // compatible values (i.e., their op must be valid).

                // Therefore, inner.oneshot0_inv_half@ cannot be HalfRightToComplete.
                // From the invariant, it must be Complete.

                // So we have inner.oneshot0_inv_half@ is Complete.
